 QualiEdge AI: On-Device Visual Inspection & Operator Advisory System

Theme: Industry and Manufacturing  
Target Hardware: Raspberry Pi 5 (Arm Cortex-A76)  

 1. Project Objective
QualiEdge AI is a zero-cloud, real-time visual inspection system designed for [PCB / Textile] manufacturing.
It detects surface anomalies using a lightweight vision model and utilizes an on-device Large Language Model (Llama 3.2 via ExecuTorch)
to provide actionable repair guidance to factory operators.

 2. Technology Stack & Justification
To ensure cost-effectiveness and high performance on edge hardware, the system relies on the following open-source stack:
*   Vision Detection: YOLO26 (Nano) – Chosen for state-of-the-art inference speed on Arm CPUs/NPUs.
      When using Hailo also:Yolov8n for max speed and YOLOv8s or YOLOv8m for Accuracy
*   Advisory Engine: Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct (4-bit Quantized) – Lightweight edge LLM providing high-quality reasoning without exhausting system RAM.
*   Runtime: ExecuTorch (XNNPACK backend) for Llama; ONNX Runtime / HailoRT for Vision.
*   Image Processing: OpenCV for handling factory noise (glare, dust reduction).

 3. System Architecture
The system employs a strict dual-pipeline isolation strategy to prevent hardware bottlenecking:

1.  Vision Pipeline (Continuous): Camera frames are captured at 30 FPS. OpenCV applies [CLAHE / Gaussian Blur] to reduce environmental noise.
YOLO11n processes every 5th frame to detect [Solder Bridges / Fabric Tears].
2.  Reasoning Pipeline (Asynchronous): Upon detecting a confirmed defect (confidence > 85% for 3 consecutive frames),
the defect metadata (class, location, severity) is passed to the ExecuTorch runtime. Llama generates a structured 2-bullet action plan for the operator.

